<title>FRANCE: Kohl-talks to continue with aims of reaching goal.</title>
<headline>Kohl-talks to continue with aims of reaching goal.</headline>
<dateline>POITIERS, France 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said on Friday that talks would continue over the weekend with aims of reaching a deal to help Europe move close to realising its goal of a currency union.</p>
<p>&quot;I am quite certain that we will find a common solution...and quite certain that we will find the right path through joint talks,&quot; Kohl said at a regular meeting with the French government.</p>
<p>This is the first time the Kohl government has met with the newly elected French government.</p>
<p>Kohl was referring to talks before next week's Amsterdam summit about Europe's currency union. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
